      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then king David sent, and brought him from the house of Machir, the son of Ammiel, from Lo-debar.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.9.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.9.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now when Mephibosheth, the son of Jonathan, the son of Saul, had come to David, he fell on his face, and did reverence. And David said, Mephibosheth. And he answered, Behold thy servant!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.9.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.9.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David said to him, Fear not: for I will surely show thee kindness for the sake of Jonathan thy father, and will restore thee all the land of Saul thy father; and thou shalt eat bread at my table continually.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.9.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.9.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he bowed himself, and said, What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy servant, that thou shouldst look upon such a dead dog as I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
